<!--
  #102: supplies, installed components, reminders and notifications — English source. Comments carry the
  ratification ids (P15-n: #15 Supplies; P47-n: #47 Installed components; P69-n: #69 a component's documents;
  P72-n: #72 loans; P79-n: #79 warranties; master plan §17 for the maintenance reminders) and what each placeholder is.

  Vocabulary: a "supply item" (SupplyItem) is a consumable or part in the owner's Supplies catalog (a filter, an oil, a
  battery); an asset "takes" it in a "role" the owner types. An "installed component" is a part fitted in an asset,
  possibly inside another one; it is "removed" (taken out on a date) or "replaced" (removed and a new one installed).
  Names, roles, part numbers, serials, units and quantities are the owner's own text and arrive as placeholders,
  unchanged. Dates arrive already formatted.

  Notifications: "maintenance due" and "overdue" reminders, a warranty warning and a loan's due-back reminder. The
  status words (DUE, OVERDUE, EXPIRES SOON, DUE BACK, NOT RETURNED) are the notification's sub-text, in capitals.
  Channel names and descriptions appear in the system's notification settings for the app.
-->
